MiiFacePartsHolder.cpp
----------------------
First PC-only include pass:

src/Game/NPC/MiiFacePartsHolder.cpp:3:10: fatal error:
Game/NPC/MiiDatabase.hpp: No such file or directory

With root headers made visible for dependency discovery, the next blockers are:

- host JKRHeap is an empty shell and cannot satisfy JKRSolidHeap/TState;
- no `operator new[](size_t, JKRSolidHeap*, int)` allocation surface;
- `MR::createDrawAdaptor` is not exposed on PC;
- `MR::isNoCalcView(const LiveActor*)` is not exposed on PC.

Further RFL_Model host audit
----------------------------
The retail model path uses indexed vertex arrays and PPC display lists. Aurora
GX has the underlying indexed-array, texture, display-list, matrix, lighting,
TEV, blend, and depth capabilities, but the RVLFace surface still needs a
host-safe bridge for PPC resource representation and `GXSetArray` data. PPC
model-resource pointers and 0x20-byte GX texture objects cannot be copied into
the current 64-bit host structs and treated as native objects.

These are compatibility-layer prerequisites. None should be worked around by
changing the recovered Game translation units.
